4. MANDATORY ATTRIBUTION & SYSTEM SIGNATURE CO-EXISTENCE
   As an explicit condition of being allowed to use this software, any 
   Android ROM image, package, or firmware built, modified, patched, or 
   ported using this software (or any derived forks) MUST comply with the 
   following:
   
   a) VISIBLE CREDIT: Credit to the original tool ("CSM by Minhmc2077") 
      must be visibly, accurately, and prominently included in all public 
      release notes, forum threads, GitHub repositories, and social media posts.
      
   b) IMMUTABLE SIGNATURE LOGIC: The core signature injected into the 
      system's properties file (specifically targeting 'ro.build.display.id' 
      in 'build.prop', or its equivalent via sed/patching) MUST NOT be 
      deleted, overwritten, obfuscated, or fully replaced. 
      
      If a derived fork modifies this tool, the final generated property 
      value MUST preserve the original authorship in a co-existence format 
      explicitly showing it is a derivative work. (e.g., "Built by 
      [YourName], powered by CSM by Minhmc2077"). Wiping the original credit 
      is strictly forbidden.

